From e982f9dad352a47cd9e2d8651990501dee342a96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:29:10 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 08/48] config: add the dist fallback switch

Kernel assembler sources that .incbin generated files fail on the
build server, because the generated file is not among the shipped
inputs. Upstream 0.19.0 reports that remote exit code to the client
as the result of the compile. The fork needs the opposite: the client
recompiles such a unit locally, so the kernel build still completes.
The two behaviours cannot share one code path without one of the
upstream remote-exit-code tests losing its assertions.

Add a boolean key `fallback` to the [dist] section of the client
configuration. It defaults to true, which keeps the fork behaviour,
and false selects the upstream 0.19.0 behaviour. This commit adds only
the key, its documentation and a unit test parsing both the explicit
value and the default; the compiler honors the key in the next
commit. Because unknown keys are denied, an older binary rejects a
configuration that contains the key, which the documentation states.

Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <floss@jetm.me>
Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
