From e01a31c69427db49a1ab0575409b4091f3e9caae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:10:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 31/48] dist: make scheduler restart safe for job accounting

A build server that keeps running across a scheduler restart can be
handed a job id it still holds a job_toolchains entry for, and
handle_assign_job asserted that the insert returned no prior value, so
the rouille worker panicked and the server answered 500. The map was
also only pruned in handle_run_job, so an assign whose run_job never
arrived leaked its entry forever.

The scheduler side of this is already covered by the random job id base
that namespaces ids per scheduler instance, so only the build server
changes here. The assign-time assert becomes a warn-and-overwrite, so a
residual collision degrades gracefully, and each job_toolchains entry is
timestamped so entries older than ABANDONED_TOOLCHAIN_TIMEOUT are swept
on each assign. Covered by test_assign_job_overwrites_stale_toolchain_entry
and test_assign_job_collects_abandoned_toolchain_entries.

Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <floss@jetm.me>
Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
