From 57ca4823938e5602aea91b9d72069d30572cf697 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:51:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 44/48] chore: fix clippy lints flagged by a newer toolchain

Clippy 1.99 rejects the tree under `-D warnings` at more sites than
the dist-specific commit covers: collapsible_if in
src/bin/sccache-dist/token_check.rs, and irregular_braces on the
`vec!(...)` calls inside the stringvec!, ovec! and pathvec! macros of
src/test/utils.rs and the vec_from! macro of tests/system.rs.

I collapsed the nested if into a let-chain and wrote the macro bodies as
`vec![...]`. Behaviour is unchanged.

The pre-commit rust-clippy hook now also allows
clippy::double_must_use. It fires on async_trait's macro expansion in
clippy 1.99 at every async trait in the crate, and there is no source
line to fix; the flag sits on the command line, next to the other -A
flags, so no allow attribute is added to the code.

Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <floss@jetm.me>
Signed-off-by: Javier Tia <javier@peridio.com>
---
